{title: 146 - I Think When I Read That Sweet Story}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #146 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 146}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bm]I [G]think when I [C/G]read [G]that sweet [Am/E]story [Em]of [D/A]old,
[D7/C]When [G]Jesus was [F#dim]here [Em]among [G]men,
[G]How [Bm]He called little [Em/B]children [G]as lambs to [C/G]His fold,
[Em/B]I should [G]like to have [D/F#]been [C/G]with [D/A]Him [Em/B]then.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bm]I [G]wish that His [C/G]hands [G]had been [Am/E]placed [Em]on my [D/A]head,
[D7/C]That [G]His arm had [F#dim]been [Em]thrown [F#dim]around [G]me,
[G]And [Bm]that I might have [Em/B]seen [B7]His [G]kind look when [C/G]He said,
[Em/B]"Let the [G]little ones [D/F#]come [C/G]unto [Em/B]Me."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bm]I [G]long for the [C/G]joy [G]of that [Am/E]glorious [Em]time,
[D7/C]The [G]sweetest and [F#dim]brightest and [G]best,
[G]When [Bm]the dear little [Em/B]children [G]of every [C/G]clime
[Em/B]Shall [G]crowd to His [D/F#]arms [C/G]and [D/A]be [Em/B]blest.
{end_of_verse}
